.179
General Info
     @0[Return to EZ-ICE]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @179[General Info]

This program performs a software front end for the Analog Devices ADSP-2100 
family fixed point Digital Signal Processor EZ-ICE.

This program is controlled by a menu driven, graphical user interface.  Items
are selected and controlled from the keyboard and/or mouse.  A menu bar at the
top of the screen provides access to windows and functions.  In addition, some
functions can be invoked directly from the keyboard whenever a special key is
pressed.  

An online help system provides help at any time simply by pressing the <F1> key
or by selecting the Help option from the menu bar.  

Further information available:

                        - @176[Help on Help System]
                        - @1[Menu Bar]
                        - @178[Special Keys]
                        - @177[Index]
               
.180
File Menu Option
     @0[Return to EZ-ICE]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @179[General Info]

This sub-menu controls file related functions of the EZ-ICE.  Choices within
this sub-menu are:

   @96[Load Executable File]      - Loads an executable file into the EZ-ICE
   @97[Load Symbol File]          - Loads a symbol file into the EZ-ICE
   @98[Load Window File]          - Loads a window file into the EZ-ICE
   @99[Save Window File]          - Saves current configuration into a file
   @103[Display File]          - Displays a text file
   @102[Playback Keystroke File]   - Replays a keystroke file
   @100[Start Keystroke Recording] - Records keystrokes to a file
   @101[Stop Keystroke Recording]  - Stops recording keystrokes to a file
   @104[Operating System Shell]    - Shells to the Operating System
   @105[Operating System Shell Command]    - Shells to the OS with a command

.181
Register Menu Option
     @0[Return to EZ-ICE]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @179[General Info]

This sub-menu controls register related functions of the EZ-ICE.  Choices 
within this sub-menu are:

   @23[Computational]           - Displays computational registers
   @23[Alternate Computational] - Displays Alternate computational registers
   @21[DAG Registers]           - Displays DAG registers 
   @31[Program Control]         - Displays program control registers
   @35[Interrupt]               - Displays interrupt control registers
   @33[Status]                  - Displays Status registers
   @29[Control]                 - Displays Control registers
   @36[PX Register]             - Displays PX Register 
   @38[Sport 0  Register]       - Displays Sport 0  Register 
   @38[Sport 1  Register]       - Displays Sport 1  Register 

.182
Memory Menu Option
     @0[Return to EZ-ICE]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @179[General Info]

This sub-menu controls register related functions of the EZ-ICE.  Choices
within this sub-menu are:

      @56[Data Memory Display]       - Displays Data Memory (DM)
         @115[Symbol Display (Alpha)] - Displays DM symbols alphabetically
         @115[Symbol Display (Num)]   - Displays DM symbols in numerical order
      @52[Program Memory Display]    - Displays Program Memory (PM)
         @110[Symbol Display (Alpha)] - Displays PM symbols alphabetically
         @110[Symbol Display (Num)]   - Displays PM symbols in numerical order
      @114[Delete Symbols]            - Deletes all symbols
      @60[Dump Memory]               - Dumps memory to a file
      @61[Load Memory]               - Loads memory from a file
      @62[Fill Memory]               - Fills memory with a pattern
      @63[Go To Address]             - Changes window to a particular address
      @64[Plot Memory]               - Plot a region of memory
      @165[Overlay memory enable]     - Enable overlay memory on EZICE board
      @166[Overlay memory disable]    - Disable overlay memory on EZICE board
      @167[Overlay memory status]     - Display current status of overlay memory

.183
Stacks Menu Option
     @0[Return to EZ-ICE]         @-1[Previous Screen]         @179[General Info]

This sub-menu controls stack related functions of the EZ-ICE.  Choices within
this sub-menu are:

               @108[Count]        - Displays Counter stack
               @106[PC]           - Displays the PC stack
               @107[Status]       - Displays the status stack

